cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it as below. It is the output of an
  autonomous AI research effort directed by Dev D. Goyal: ChatGPT (OpenAI,
  GPT-6 with Pro reasoning) produced the proofs and the Lean formalization,
  and Claude Opus 5.5, used with Claude Code, verified them independently
  and rewrote the papers. See AUTHORSHIP.md for details.
title: >-
  Proofs and corrections for 34 OEIS entries, with Lean 4 formalizations
  (an autonomous AI research effort)
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Goyal
    given-names: Dev D.
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-24
repository-code: "https://github.com/dvgyl/oeis-a396843-proof"
abstract: >-
  Self-contained papers, Lean 4 formal proofs, and independent numerical
  checks for 34 entries of the On-Line Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences.
  Across 23 newly targeted entries, 38 conjectured statements are proved and
  2 are shown to be false and corrected; the original problem (A396843,
  A396844) is solved, including corrected residue classifications; 8 known
  results receive self-contained proofs and formalizations; and one
  elementary observation is proved. The mathematics and formalization were
  generated autonomously by ChatGPT (OpenAI, GPT-6 with Pro reasoning) from
  prompts by Dev D. Goyal; Claude Opus 5.5, used with Claude Code, rebuilt
  and audited the Lean proofs, checked every claim numerically against
  current OEIS data, rewrote the papers for readability, and organized the
  repository. The
  work has not been peer reviewed, and no priority is claimed.
keywords:
  - integer sequences
  - OEIS
  - formal power series
  - congruences
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - AI-generated mathematics
references:
